{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he sent them, etc.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to say this, given that the sending has already been mentioned twice: ״וַיִּשְׁלַח אוֹתָם״ (Numbers 13:3), ״אֲשֶׁר שָׁלַח מֹשֶׁה״ (Numbers 13:16)? And perhaps the verse informs us that he provided them with an escort, and the verse gives the reason for the escort and says <b>to spy out</b>, etc. — for they needed protection because they were traveling a dangerous road. It further intends that the escort was for the road they would spy out, for such is the nature of an escort."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:18.268548025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}